# Line-ending policy.
#
# Deliberately targeted rather than `* text=auto`: nine tracked files are
# binary and every one of them carries stray \r bytes inside its payload, so
# a blanket normalisation risks rewriting their contents.

# Shell-executed files must keep LF. A .sh with CRLF makes BusyBox and dash
# abort immediately, and makes bash run on with `set -eu` never in effect.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
Dockerfile.*    text eol=lf

# Shell-parsed configuration: a trailing \r lands inside the variable value.
env.sample      text eol=lf
*.template      text eol=lf

# Run by the postgres container's entrypoint at init.
*.sql           text eol=lf

# Binary: never normalise, never diff as text. These are the extensions
# actually tracked here (*.png is 6 files; the others one each).
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.ico           binary
*.lockb         binary
